From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] evr: an unknown CLSID in DllGetClassObject is not an unimplemented feature (WARN, not FIXME)

IClassFactory::LockServer was already made a quiet S_OK by 2837. An unknown CLSID passed
to DllGetClassObject returns CLASS_E_CLASSNOTAVAILABLE as documented; it is logged
with WARN instead of FIXME (it is not an unimplemented feature).
---
diff --git a/dlls/evr/main.c b/dlls/evr/main.c
index 25c27c7..c1d9a60 100644
--- a/dlls/evr/main.c
+++ b/dlls/evr/main.c
@@ -167,7 +167,11 @@ HRESULT WINAPI DllGetClassObject(REFCLSID rclsid, REFIID riid, void **out)
 
     if (i == ARRAY_SIZE(object_creation))
     {
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_NOCLASS_FIXME
         FIXME("%s: no class found.\n", debugstr_guid(rclsid));
+#else
+        WARN("%s: no class found.\n", debugstr_guid(rclsid));
+#endif
         return CLASS_E_CLASSNOTAVAILABLE;
     }
 
